rom the note edge  where you can have information scroll  across the edge when it's sitting face  up or at night you can dimly show the  time on that amoled display makes sense  obviously that's not new then the people  edge is a constantly available swipe in  from the upper right sort of natural for  the thumb to bring in your most  frequently contacted people for a  one-touch phone call or email and this  is kinda cool but i really wish samsung  would have let us put anything there  like our five favorite apps or something  that would have been a legit useful  feature but for now it's just contacts  can't really change that  and you'll notice the little circle  rings around the contact names those are  actually connected with edge lighting so  when your phone is facing down and you  receive a call from one of those people  it lights up the edges of your phone  with the color of the person calling and  of course that lights up the table it's  on too it gives you a pretty good idea  of who's calling before you have to turn  it over pretty neat look not one of  those things that blows my mind but at  least it's good looking  but yeah other than that the edge  display is all about immersion that's  really what impressed me the most i just  couldn't stop looking at this damn  display it got this weird not really  distortion to it but you know viewing  angles don't suffer but it has this  different look on the edges i don't know  it's weird reflections look different  also i don't know if it was intentional  or not but with all these new android  apps that swipe in from the left hand  side this display is kind of perfect for  pulling in those drawers again i don't  know if samsung did that on purpose but  it's a really nice feeling and a sort of  a dope side effect from having these  curved over edges with the glass and i  can guarantee you won't see any other  phone with this shape out there so it's  a unique form factor it's something  different and new  i think now t